# roastmesh rendezvous hosts -- always-on nodes for fast peer discovery.
#
# Fetched at startup (net.serve(), when --wan-discovery is on) from
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Carlsans/roastmesh/master/BOOTSTRAP_NODES
# and hello'd directly, bypassing the public BitTorrent DHT lookup entirely --
# see src/roastmesh/bootstrap.py and ARCHITECTURE.md's "Peer discovery"
# section for why. Editing this file changes what every roastmesh install
# tries first, without anyone needing to update their binary.
#
# Format: one host per line, blank lines and "#" comments ignored.
#   host
#   host,literal-ip-fallback
#   host,literal-ip-fallback,port
# The literal IP is used only if DNS fails to resolve the host; port
# defaults to WAN_PORT (41890) when omitted.

moduloinfo.ca
